1
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,011
To my beloved wife.

2
00:00:07,545 --> 00:00:10,882
It has been two months
since you left home.

3
00:00:10,949 --> 00:00:11,716
Hey, wait a minute!

4
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:16,020
The other day, a student requested
I be replaced as homeroom teacher,

5
00:00:16,087 --> 00:00:18,990
but I resolved that crisis,
and I feel like…

6
00:00:19,057 --> 00:00:23,695
I'm steadily becoming a Great Teacher.

7
00:00:23,761 --> 00:00:26,164
However, one thing still concerns me.

8
00:00:26,731 --> 00:00:30,568
A scholarship student of mine
in the soccer club got badly injured.

9
00:00:32,103 --> 00:00:33,138
Please do not run.

10
00:00:33,771 --> 00:00:34,706
Sorry.

11
00:00:36,674 --> 00:00:38,376
CENTRAL TREATMENT ROOM

12
00:00:38,443 --> 00:00:39,711
Oh, excuse me.

13
00:00:40,278 --> 00:00:41,913
Hiroto! You okay?

14
00:00:42,514 --> 00:00:43,815
Oh, I'm sorry.

15
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,652
Why are you here, Ms. Koizumi?

16
00:00:48,353 --> 00:00:50,588
I'm the soccer club advisor.
Surprising, huh?

17
00:00:51,823 --> 00:00:52,857
I see.

18
00:00:53,358 --> 00:00:55,593
So how is Hiroto?

19
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:02,133
He has a compound fracture
in his left hand,

20
00:01:02,834 --> 00:01:05,703
and it seems he won't be able
to play the rest of the year.

21
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:07,438
-What, that long?
-Shut up!

22
00:01:12,343 --> 00:01:14,312
Hiroto, are you okay?

23
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,114
Yes.

24
00:01:17,782 --> 00:01:19,584
Cheer up, come on.

25
00:01:20,318 --> 00:01:23,054
You're still a first-year,
so there's always next year…

26
00:01:23,621 --> 00:01:24,522
What?

27
00:01:25,256 --> 00:01:26,157
What do you mean?

28
00:01:26,224 --> 00:01:27,559
He doesn't know yet.

29
00:01:29,694 --> 00:01:31,429
No, what I mean is…

30
00:01:31,496 --> 00:01:33,698
I'll leave the details to Ms. Koizumi.

31
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:37,001
I'll go buy you something. Okay?

32
00:01:37,702 --> 00:01:38,937
Excuse me.

33
00:01:42,874 --> 00:01:46,377
Hiroto, I spoke with the doctor earlier.

34
00:01:46,945 --> 00:01:49,647
It looks like you'll have
a cast for a while.

35
00:01:49,714 --> 00:01:52,383
Things will probably be tough from now on,

36
00:01:53,084 --> 00:01:56,688
but as long as I stay by his side,
I'm sure it will be fine.

37
00:01:56,754 --> 00:01:59,791
Because I believe a Great Teacher

38
00:02:00,458 --> 00:02:03,761
isn't someone who immediately tries
to find a solution,

39
00:02:04,329 --> 00:02:06,831
but one who first empathizes
with the students

40
00:02:06,898 --> 00:02:09,534
and always stands by them.

41
00:02:11,336 --> 00:02:14,105
All right, this one's got to work!

42
00:02:15,306 --> 00:02:16,241
What?

43
00:02:16,941 --> 00:02:18,910
WONDERFUL ANSWER

44
00:02:18,977 --> 00:02:22,914
Awesome! She's going to come back to me!

45
00:02:23,881 --> 00:02:24,716
What?

46
00:02:24,782 --> 00:02:26,784
BUT IT SOUNDS LIKE YOU GOT IT
FROM SOMEONE ELSE

47
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:27,752
Damn…

48
00:02:28,386 --> 00:02:30,989
Why are you so sharp?

49
00:02:32,156 --> 00:02:33,424
Good morning.

50
00:02:35,326 --> 00:02:36,728
Is something wrong?

51
00:02:37,295 --> 00:02:38,463
No, nothing.

52
00:02:39,063 --> 00:02:40,999
We don't have enough members!

53
00:02:41,065 --> 00:02:42,433
Good morning, everyone.

54
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,901
Good morning.

55
00:02:43,968 --> 00:02:45,470
Take your seats, come on.

56
00:02:46,437 --> 00:02:49,440
Let's make today a good day too.

57
00:02:50,275 --> 00:02:51,843
Oh, that's right.

58
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:55,146
I visited Hiroto in the hospital,
and he seemed down,

59
00:02:55,213 --> 00:02:57,548
so once he's discharged,
let's all cheer him up.

60
00:02:57,615 --> 00:02:58,549
Right on!

61
00:02:59,284 --> 00:03:00,985
That means, "Got it."

62
00:03:08,026 --> 00:03:09,460
What is it, Mr. Onizuka?

63
00:03:09,527 --> 00:03:12,397
Oh, nothing, it just suddenly hit me.

64
00:03:13,598 --> 00:03:17,302
At first, when I became the homeroom
teacher, no one looked at me.

65
00:03:17,368 --> 00:03:20,238
But now, lots of you are looking at me!

66
00:03:21,873 --> 00:03:25,176
But for the sake of everyone
who hasn't given me a high rating yet,

67
00:03:25,777 --> 00:03:27,912
I'll do my best as your homeroom teacher,

68
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:31,783
so if you ever have any problems,
tell me, don't be shy!

69
00:03:33,084 --> 00:03:34,252
Okay?

70
00:04:59,337 --> 00:05:01,239
I'm so busy, busy…

71
00:05:01,305 --> 00:05:02,707
Look at this!

72
00:05:02,774 --> 00:05:06,411
Over half of my class
have given me a good rating!

73
00:05:06,477 --> 00:05:07,478
What?

74
00:05:07,545 --> 00:05:11,549
At this rate, I'll get
a winter bonus, right?

75
00:05:11,616 --> 00:05:12,917
ONIZUKA EIKICHI
RATINGS - 15 OF 28

76
00:05:12,984 --> 00:05:14,485
GOOD RATINGS - 15 OF 28

77
00:05:14,552 --> 00:05:16,454
I'm sure it will go down soon enough.

78
00:05:16,521 --> 00:05:18,856
Don't say that, come on.

79
00:05:18,923 --> 00:05:19,824
Vice Principal.

80
00:05:19,891 --> 00:05:23,194
-You should acknowledge my abilities…
-You're annoying, go away!

81
00:05:23,895 --> 00:05:26,998
Still, how could that man
be more popular than me?

82
00:05:27,565 --> 00:05:30,868
Mr. Abe, why don't you try
using nicknames with the students too?

83
00:05:30,935 --> 00:05:33,504
What? Why would I need to do that?

84
00:05:33,571 --> 00:05:34,505
Abechan!

85
00:05:34,572 --> 00:05:36,774
It was only for a short time, but thanks.

86
00:05:37,341 --> 00:05:40,144
Thanks for taking care
of our Itsuki Fukuda.

87
00:05:40,211 --> 00:05:42,713
I'm sorry, but could you stop
calling me "Abechan"?

88
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:45,383
Oh, would you prefer
another nickname? Like Abecchi?

89
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:46,884
I can't understand you at all.

90
00:05:49,854 --> 00:05:53,591
Ms. Koizumi,
do you mind if I call you by a nickname?

91
00:05:54,325 --> 00:05:57,662
I have no problem with it at all.
It's totally normal overseas.

92
00:05:57,728 --> 00:06:00,364
Truly our most popular teacher.
So easygoing!

93
00:06:01,332 --> 00:06:02,200
Oh, what?

94
00:06:02,266 --> 00:06:04,469
I think your good ratings
are dropping a bit!

95
00:06:05,937 --> 00:06:09,941
At this rate, it might just be a matter
of time before I overtake you.

96
00:06:10,007 --> 00:06:11,342
Ms. Koizumi, you're in a pinch!

97
00:06:12,577 --> 00:06:14,645
I don't mind at all. Go ahead.

98
00:06:14,712 --> 00:06:16,447
Become our number one!

99
00:06:20,017 --> 00:06:22,487
Everyone, what were you talking about?

100
00:06:23,488 --> 00:06:24,155
Hey!

101
00:06:25,022 --> 00:06:26,991
Who is in charge of this high school?

102
00:06:27,058 --> 00:06:30,328
-I am…
-It's me, the Vice-Principal. Go ahead.

103
00:06:30,394 --> 00:06:32,730
What is wrong with this school?

104
00:06:33,231 --> 00:06:37,068
You gravely hurt my dear son,
and didn't even apologize?

105
00:06:37,134 --> 00:06:40,271
Mr. Hosokawa, we offered an apology
to your wife yesterday.

106
00:06:40,338 --> 00:06:42,106
I haven't heard a thing about it!

107
00:06:42,173 --> 00:06:43,241
If I remember correctly,

108
00:06:43,808 --> 00:06:46,777
despite being a woman,
you're the soccer club advisor, right?

109
00:06:46,844 --> 00:06:49,514
Why didn't you properly educate
the other students?

110
00:06:50,281 --> 00:06:53,718
Settle down. I believe Ms. Koizumi
is a teacher with great enthusiasm.

111
00:06:53,784 --> 00:06:54,685
You too!

112
00:06:55,686 --> 00:06:59,891
Do you even understand how special
Hiroto is to this high school?

113
00:06:59,957 --> 00:07:03,961
Without him, there's no way
you'll win the soccer tournament!

114
00:07:04,028 --> 00:07:07,131
I just remembered, I have some
personal business to attend to.

115
00:07:07,198 --> 00:07:09,367
The principal will handle this
in my place.

116
00:07:09,433 --> 00:07:11,836
What? Hey, Vice Principal!

117
00:07:11,903 --> 00:07:12,737
Hey.

118
00:07:12,803 --> 00:07:14,872
How are you going to discipline them?

119
00:07:15,439 --> 00:07:17,108
The ones who injured my son.

120
00:07:17,174 --> 00:07:21,746
But I don't think
they did it out of malice either.

121
00:07:21,812 --> 00:07:22,747
What did you say?

122
00:07:22,813 --> 00:07:25,149
Then what if something
similar happens again?

123
00:07:25,883 --> 00:07:29,287
Times like this make you
want to quit being a teacher.

124
00:07:29,353 --> 00:07:32,189
That man is quite famous
for being a toxic parent.

125
00:07:32,256 --> 00:07:33,858
He used to play in the J-League,

126
00:07:33,925 --> 00:07:37,161
so he meddles in every little thing
related to his son's training.

127
00:07:37,228 --> 00:07:38,763
We are the victims here!

128
00:07:38,829 --> 00:07:40,431
It can't be helped then.

129
00:07:42,466 --> 00:07:44,468
I'm going to give it to him straight.

130
00:07:44,535 --> 00:07:45,369
What?

131
00:07:45,436 --> 00:07:46,971
How will you deal with them?

132
00:07:47,038 --> 00:07:51,142
Hey, come on now, sir.
Calm down for a moment.

133
00:07:51,208 --> 00:07:52,443
Who the hell are you?

134
00:07:53,210 --> 00:07:56,213
I'm Eikichi Onizuka,
Hiroto's homeroom teacher.

135
00:07:57,248 --> 00:07:58,549
So it's you!

136
00:07:58,616 --> 00:08:03,588
My son was talking about how his teacher
is a low-rated, analog, delusional man!

137
00:08:03,654 --> 00:08:06,190
With all due respect, right now,

138
00:08:06,257 --> 00:08:09,293
my popularity is soaring,
and I've received good ratings

139
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,895
from more than half the class.

140
00:08:10,962 --> 00:08:13,764
More importantly, what do you plan to do?

141
00:08:13,831 --> 00:08:15,600
How will you take responsibility?

142
00:08:15,666 --> 00:08:17,768
About that, well…

143
00:08:18,336 --> 00:08:21,472
Could you give us a little time?

144
00:08:21,539 --> 00:08:24,709
We haven't heard the full story
from the soccer club members.

145
00:08:25,776 --> 00:08:27,345
Please rest assured.

146
00:08:27,411 --> 00:08:29,513
I will do right by you, sir.

147
00:08:30,014 --> 00:08:32,383
You guys keep half-assing your job!

148
00:08:32,450 --> 00:08:34,619
Do it properly!

149
00:08:35,286 --> 00:08:38,522
That guy is a standard pushy parent.

150
00:08:38,589 --> 00:08:41,359
But are you sure
you should have said what you did?

151
00:08:41,425 --> 00:08:44,228
It's fine. If he comes barging in
yelling again,

152
00:08:44,295 --> 00:08:46,931
I'll take him out for a drink,
then we'll be like,

153
00:08:46,998 --> 00:08:49,767
"Hey, don't we actually
get along super well?"

154
00:08:49,834 --> 00:08:53,804
Most of the time,
that gets them to settle down.

155
00:08:53,871 --> 00:08:57,141
Don't tell me you did that
at your previous schools too?

156
00:08:57,842 --> 00:08:59,110
Yes, is there a problem?

157
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:01,145
No, not really.

158
00:09:01,212 --> 00:09:02,346
I'm going for a smoke.

159
00:09:08,486 --> 00:09:11,355
What did that Onizuka guy
say he was going to do?

160
00:09:11,422 --> 00:09:13,824
It was quite vague.

161
00:09:13,891 --> 00:09:16,460
It seems like he'll cause
even more trouble.

162
00:09:17,662 --> 00:09:20,498
But this might actually be an opportunity.

163
00:09:21,332 --> 00:09:23,267
If the problem gets complicated

164
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:26,637
and Onizuka uses violence
against that father,

165
00:09:26,704 --> 00:09:30,474
we can make him take responsibility
and end his tenure here.

166
00:09:30,541 --> 00:09:31,409
What?

167
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:35,246
Wouldn't that be more convenient
for you too, Miss?

168
00:09:36,714 --> 00:09:39,617
You won't have to worry about him
taking your spot as number one.

169
00:09:45,189 --> 00:09:48,893
-Ken-Ken, quit giggling!
-Yuukichi, aren't you being too strict?

170
00:09:48,959 --> 00:09:49,827
Hero pose…

171
00:09:49,894 --> 00:09:51,028
Oh, Hiroto!

172
00:09:51,095 --> 00:09:51,962
Hiroto!

173
00:09:52,029 --> 00:09:53,464
You're out!

174
00:09:53,531 --> 00:09:54,398
What?

175
00:09:54,465 --> 00:09:56,367
Congrats on being discharged!

176
00:09:56,434 --> 00:09:59,270
I heard you can't play soccer
for a while. Are you okay?

177
00:09:59,804 --> 00:10:00,638
Yeah…

178
00:10:00,705 --> 00:10:02,239
Why not join our Drill Team?

179
00:10:02,807 --> 00:10:03,607
What?

180
00:10:03,674 --> 00:10:06,711
Please! With just one more person,
we can officially become a club.

181
00:10:06,777 --> 00:10:10,514
Itsuki turned us down,
so we're at a standstill.

182
00:10:10,581 --> 00:10:14,652
Sorry, but unlike you guys,
I don't join clubs half-heartedly.

183
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:16,053
What?

184
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,722
Hey, what's with the attitude?

185
00:10:17,788 --> 00:10:21,425
Yeah, we were just worrying
about you since we're classmates.

186
00:10:21,492 --> 00:10:24,395
Once I graduate from high school,

187
00:10:24,462 --> 00:10:27,264
I'll live in a completely
different world from you all.

188
00:10:28,132 --> 00:10:31,469
STAFF ROOM

189
00:10:33,537 --> 00:10:34,839
Oh, Hiroto!

190
00:10:36,173 --> 00:10:38,442
Congratulations on being discharged.

191
00:10:39,744 --> 00:10:40,711
Hiroto.

192
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:45,416
Sorry it's sudden, but we need to talk.
Come to the club after school.

193
00:10:46,317 --> 00:10:47,151
Sure, but…

194
00:10:47,218 --> 00:10:49,153
I'll come with him.

195
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:51,922
No need. This is our soccer club's issue.

196
00:10:51,989 --> 00:10:52,923
Is that so?

197
00:10:57,061 --> 00:10:58,796
Hiroto will…

198
00:10:58,863 --> 00:10:59,697
Hiroto!

199
00:11:04,101 --> 00:11:06,937
Let's have the member
who caused the injury apologize.

200
00:11:07,004 --> 00:11:07,972
Yes.

201
00:11:11,909 --> 00:11:15,146
Hiroto, I'm sorry
things turned out like this.

202
00:11:17,214 --> 00:11:20,317
Hiroto, he didn't mean any harm,

203
00:11:20,384 --> 00:11:23,220
so why don't we all
work together and do our best?

204
00:11:25,523 --> 00:11:26,724
I don't mind…

205
00:11:27,525 --> 00:11:30,361
but without me can you even make it
to the year-end tournament?

206
00:11:30,427 --> 00:11:31,262
What?

207
00:11:31,328 --> 00:11:33,798
Well, if the team comes together as one--

208
00:11:33,864 --> 00:11:36,033
If you have time to say such things,

209
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,703
try to make sure our team members
don't injure each other!

210
00:11:40,704 --> 00:11:41,972
And besides,

211
00:11:42,807 --> 00:11:44,809
even if I keep the opponent
from scoring goals…

212
00:11:45,409 --> 00:11:47,411
-You can't score anyway!
-Hey!

213
00:11:48,212 --> 00:11:49,947
How dare you talk
to your seniors like that?

214
00:11:50,014 --> 00:11:51,749
You're talented, but too arrogant!

215
00:11:51,816 --> 00:11:52,850
Hey…

216
00:11:52,917 --> 00:11:55,119
-He's right!
-You're cocky!

217
00:11:55,186 --> 00:11:56,787
Wait, everyone, calm down!

218
00:11:58,189 --> 00:12:01,559
We can't play with a guy like him anymore.

219
00:12:01,625 --> 00:12:03,661
-It's impossible.
-Yeah!

220
00:12:03,727 --> 00:12:07,264
That's right!
It's all Hiroto's fault! Repent!

221
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:09,934
Mr. Onizuka, why are you here?

222
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,037
Sorry, I was a bit concerned.

223
00:12:14,505 --> 00:12:15,339
Hiroto,

224
00:12:16,774 --> 00:12:19,343
you know that you
can't play soccer alone, right?

225
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:22,813
Why don't you apologize to everyone?

226
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:27,685
I'm the one who got injured,
so why do I have to apologize?

227
00:12:28,886 --> 00:12:31,222
Your injury and this are unrelated, right?

228
00:12:32,122 --> 00:12:35,226
What I want to teach is
the importance of having teammates.

229
00:12:35,292 --> 00:12:39,230
I don't think of them
as my teammates anyway.

230
00:12:39,296 --> 00:12:40,264
What?

231
00:12:40,331 --> 00:12:43,534
Why talk like that?
You're just like your father.

232
00:12:43,601 --> 00:12:44,869
I see.

233
00:12:46,570 --> 00:12:49,106
Fine then, I'm quitting the soccer team!

234
00:12:50,441 --> 00:12:51,375
Hiroto!

235
00:12:51,442 --> 00:12:53,043
Good luck with that!

236
00:12:54,678 --> 00:12:55,980
Without me,

237
00:12:56,714 --> 00:12:58,782
I don't think you can beat anyone.

238
00:13:03,153 --> 00:13:05,289
Why did you have to butt in?

239
00:13:05,356 --> 00:13:08,092
Now the problem's gotten
even more complicated!

240
00:13:08,158 --> 00:13:11,862
I just wanted to say that if you do
something bad, you should apologize.

241
00:13:12,429 --> 00:13:17,167
Do you think such childlike logic
can convince that boy and his father?

242
00:13:17,234 --> 00:13:18,469
What is it?

243
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:21,405
What are you two talking about?

244
00:13:22,106 --> 00:13:25,175
Oh right, about the soccer
scholarship student…

245
00:13:25,242 --> 00:13:27,044
Hey, that hurts!

246
00:13:27,111 --> 00:13:28,712
-What?
-Hey.

247
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:32,249
Why is my son quitting the soccer club?

248
00:13:32,316 --> 00:13:33,851
Um, that is…

249
00:13:33,918 --> 00:13:36,487
Come on, sir, calm down.

250
00:13:36,553 --> 00:13:40,257
Why don't we go for a drink
and have a talk?

251
00:13:40,324 --> 00:13:41,358
What?

252
00:13:41,425 --> 00:13:44,762
Such an irresponsible attitude
for your age. Are you really a teacher?

253
00:13:44,828 --> 00:13:45,796
No, I mean…

254
00:13:45,863 --> 00:13:48,866
You're absolutely right, Mr. Hosokawa.

255
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:51,702
Ever since he was young,

256
00:13:51,769 --> 00:13:55,806
this man has been ignoring policies
and repeating selfish behavior…

257
00:13:55,873 --> 00:13:58,776
Then why make a guy like him
my son's homeroom teacher?

258
00:13:58,842 --> 00:14:01,312
So, including that too,

259
00:14:01,378 --> 00:14:03,981
we will hold an emergency
parents' meeting,

260
00:14:04,048 --> 00:14:05,783
to explain everything.

261
00:14:05,849 --> 00:14:07,051
Emergency parents' meeting?

262
00:14:07,117 --> 00:14:11,021
Yes, we will make this man explain
everything thoroughly.

263
00:14:13,590 --> 00:14:15,225
Good morning.

264
00:14:15,292 --> 00:14:16,994
Good morning, go ahead.

265
00:14:18,295 --> 00:14:20,431
Aren't you worried?

266
00:14:20,497 --> 00:14:22,032
Not at all.

267
00:14:22,099 --> 00:14:25,436
I've gone through things like this
tons of times before.

268
00:14:25,502 --> 00:14:27,171
I see.

269
00:14:28,205 --> 00:14:33,377
First, we would like to hear
everyone's candid opinions

270
00:14:33,444 --> 00:14:35,946
about the homeroom teacher, Mr. Onizuka.

271
00:14:36,013 --> 00:14:37,982
My son says that

272
00:14:38,682 --> 00:14:42,586
since that man became homeroom teacher,
he hasn't been able to focus on soccer.

273
00:14:42,653 --> 00:14:44,154
No, that's not…

274
00:14:44,989 --> 00:14:46,523
So that's how it was.

275
00:14:46,590 --> 00:14:48,859
Even so, that man,

276
00:14:49,493 --> 00:14:52,029
instead of comforting my injured son,

277
00:14:52,096 --> 00:14:54,231
he yelled at him
in front of the club members!

278
00:14:54,298 --> 00:14:55,666
No, I didn't…

279
00:14:55,733 --> 00:14:59,503
We are extremely sorry.

280
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:04,842
Because he's a former biker gang member,
my daughter said he's kind of scary.

281
00:15:04,908 --> 00:15:08,812
My child also said he almost forced
a nickname on them.

282
00:15:11,048 --> 00:15:14,618
Hey, why did you hire
such a problematic teacher

283
00:15:14,685 --> 00:15:17,254
without even asking for our opinions?

284
00:15:17,321 --> 00:15:18,155
He's right.

285
00:15:18,222 --> 00:15:20,858
Well, that's due to…

286
00:15:20,924 --> 00:15:26,230
the policy of the parent company
that manages our school, so to speak…

287
00:15:28,499 --> 00:15:30,167
Great timing.

288
00:15:30,234 --> 00:15:33,437
Mr. Miyazawa, an employee
from the company, is here,

289
00:15:33,504 --> 00:15:37,741
so let's have him explain
the circumstances behind his hiring.

290
00:15:37,808 --> 00:15:39,943
-What?
-If you please!

291
00:15:41,345 --> 00:15:42,613
Right.

292
00:15:48,185 --> 00:15:49,186
Um…

293
00:15:50,387 --> 00:15:52,523
My name is Ryunosuke Miyazawa.

294
00:15:53,290 --> 00:15:57,561
Actually, I used to be one of
Mr. Onizuka's students, so I understand.

295
00:15:58,695 --> 00:16:01,932
It's easy to misunderstand him at first,
but despite how he looks,

296
00:16:01,999 --> 00:16:05,135
he cares about the students
more than anyone else.

297
00:16:05,202 --> 00:16:08,839
Hey, are you saying
that we don't care about our children?

298
00:16:08,906 --> 00:16:11,075
No, I didn't mean it that way.

299
00:16:12,376 --> 00:16:13,477
I believe Mr. Onizuka…

300
00:16:14,111 --> 00:16:18,315
can teach today's children
the important things

301
00:16:18,382 --> 00:16:20,717
that we adults fail to properly convey.

302
00:16:20,784 --> 00:16:22,519
Don't speak so pretentiously!

303
00:16:22,586 --> 00:16:25,889
Even without a guy like him,
we are perfectly decent parents!

304
00:16:25,956 --> 00:16:27,291
No, but…

305
00:16:27,357 --> 00:16:29,526
Calm down, everyone…

306
00:16:29,593 --> 00:16:31,595
The reason our school

307
00:16:31,662 --> 00:16:36,100
has been forced to leave
Mr. Onizuka alone until now is because,

308
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:39,002
while his educational philosophy
differs from ours,

309
00:16:39,069 --> 00:16:42,039
he was producing results in his own way.

310
00:16:42,106 --> 00:16:47,010
However, his handling
of this situation was unacceptable.

311
00:16:47,077 --> 00:16:50,414
Then fire him immediately!

312
00:16:50,481 --> 00:16:54,251
If only he were an excellent
homeroom teacher, like Ms. Koizumi.

313
00:16:54,318 --> 00:16:57,621
I can't send my child to school
with peace of mind.

314
00:16:57,688 --> 00:17:00,224
What are you going to do, calling us here…

315
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:01,725
Well, well.

316
00:17:01,792 --> 00:17:04,194
Excuse me, everyone,

317
00:17:04,828 --> 00:17:08,532
shouldn't we also hear
Mr. Onizuka's opinion?

318
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:11,702
I'm sure he will
reflect on himself and apologize.

319
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:15,005
So, Mr. Onizuka?

320
00:17:15,672 --> 00:17:17,274
Everyone,

321
00:17:18,175 --> 00:17:20,511
thank you for taking the time
to come today.

322
00:17:28,852 --> 00:17:34,191
To begin with,
schools are basically full of problems.

323
00:17:35,192 --> 00:17:39,429
I mean, it would be weirder if you crammed
teenage kids into a classroom

324
00:17:39,496 --> 00:17:40,831
and no problems occurred!

325
00:17:41,999 --> 00:17:48,338
High schoolers have always been proud,
cheeky brats, but recently,

326
00:17:48,405 --> 00:17:52,176
they gather information through social
media and have come to look down

327
00:17:52,242 --> 00:17:54,044
on us adults more and more.

328
00:17:54,645 --> 00:17:58,282
And the adults who walk on eggshells
around brats like that are wrong!

329
00:18:00,317 --> 00:18:01,451
Hey.

330
00:18:02,553 --> 00:18:03,887
What are you saying?

331
00:18:04,388 --> 00:18:07,057
You're not reflecting on anything,
you bastard!

332
00:18:07,124 --> 00:18:10,294
Hey, don't call people "bastard"!

333
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,362
It's because he has a father like you

334
00:18:12,930 --> 00:18:16,800
that Hiroto grew up to be someone
who doesn't understand people's feelings!

335
00:18:16,867 --> 00:18:19,002
Hey, don't mess with me.

336
00:18:19,069 --> 00:18:20,771
-Vice Principal!
-Yes.

337
00:18:20,837 --> 00:18:23,774
Fire him as soon as possible!

338
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:25,842
How about you look at yourself first?

339
00:18:25,909 --> 00:18:28,812
You probably talk down to staff

340
00:18:28,879 --> 00:18:31,582
at places like taxis
or restaurants, don't you?

341
00:18:31,648 --> 00:18:33,417
Do you realize

342
00:18:33,483 --> 00:18:38,155
that you shouldn't show that kind
of behavior in front of your child?

343
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:40,057
What's with you?

344
00:18:40,557 --> 00:18:42,726
-Try saying that one more time, punk!
-You want to go?

345
00:18:47,998 --> 00:18:49,933
I'll never forgive this! You bastard!

346
00:18:55,239 --> 00:18:57,841
One, two!

347
00:18:57,908 --> 00:19:00,744
Good morning.

348
00:19:01,678 --> 00:19:02,613
Mr. Onizuka.

349
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:04,448
Do you have a moment?

350
00:19:04,514 --> 00:19:05,582
What is it?

351
00:19:08,252 --> 00:19:10,654
I discussed it
with the Vice Principal too.

352
00:19:13,023 --> 00:19:16,026
Could you refrain from
attending classes for the time being?

353
00:19:16,093 --> 00:19:18,462
What? Why?

354
00:19:18,528 --> 00:19:21,231
Well, there was the incident yesterday,

355
00:19:21,298 --> 00:19:24,268
and if there's no punishment whatsoever,

356
00:19:24,334 --> 00:19:27,537
the parents won't be satisfied.

357
00:19:27,604 --> 00:19:28,705
During that time,

358
00:19:28,772 --> 00:19:32,209
you should carefully consider
your own future plans.

359
00:19:32,776 --> 00:19:35,145
Why do I have to do something like that?

360
00:19:35,212 --> 00:19:37,314
If things remain like this forever,

361
00:19:37,381 --> 00:19:40,150
that father will come
barging in every day,

362
00:19:40,217 --> 00:19:42,419
and the other teachers
won't be able to work.

363
00:19:43,854 --> 00:19:45,422
Well, then,

364
00:19:45,489 --> 00:19:48,392
what must happen for Mr. Onizuka
to be able to return?

365
00:19:48,458 --> 00:19:50,694
-About that--
-Let's see…

366
00:19:50,761 --> 00:19:54,364
He can return if that father
accepts him as the homeroom teacher.

367
00:19:55,132 --> 00:19:58,201
I think pigs would fly
before that happens, though!

368
00:19:59,269 --> 00:20:03,173
Right, everyone, homeroom is starting.

369
00:20:06,977 --> 00:20:08,412
Ms. Koizumi.

370
00:20:09,079 --> 00:20:10,080
Yes?

371
00:20:10,147 --> 00:20:12,182
Why did you do that?

372
00:20:12,949 --> 00:20:14,051
What do you mean?

373
00:20:14,117 --> 00:20:17,354
In the parents' meeting,
you intentionally passed the conversation

374
00:20:17,421 --> 00:20:19,723
to Mr. Onizuka to make him apologize.

375
00:20:19,790 --> 00:20:22,693
Even though you knew
it would cause further trouble.

376
00:20:24,127 --> 00:20:26,063
I don't know what you're talking about.

377
00:20:27,097 --> 00:20:28,899
Was it just my misunderstanding?

378
00:20:30,434 --> 00:20:31,668
What was?

379
00:20:32,202 --> 00:20:35,605
When I was newly appointed,
you were my instructor,

380
00:20:35,672 --> 00:20:37,374
and you gave me lots of advice.

381
00:20:38,375 --> 00:20:42,713
Even now, I remember you said that
when students ask a question,

382
00:20:42,779 --> 00:20:46,483
it's good to ask a question back,
as much as possible.

383
00:20:47,384 --> 00:20:51,154
You said, if you ask things like, "What
do you think?" or, "Why do you think so?"

384
00:20:51,822 --> 00:20:55,759
the children's ability
to think will deepen.

385
00:20:57,127 --> 00:21:00,397
At that time, I thought to myself,

386
00:21:02,566 --> 00:21:08,038
"This person truly believes
in the power of education."

387
00:21:08,105 --> 00:21:11,074
I think that's also
why the students like you.

388
00:21:14,945 --> 00:21:16,980
Did such a thing happen?

389
00:21:25,689 --> 00:21:27,057
What is it?

390
00:21:27,124 --> 00:21:31,962
There's this extremely long word,
do you know it?

391
00:21:38,001 --> 00:21:40,904
It means "the action of regarding
something as worthless.

392
00:21:40,971 --> 00:21:42,939
To look down on. Treat with contempt."

393
00:21:44,341 --> 00:21:48,044
Are you trying to say
I'm doing that to the others?

394
00:21:48,111 --> 00:21:52,382
No, that's not it,
but because you have talent,

395
00:21:52,449 --> 00:21:57,187
your demands toward the other members
end up becoming like orders.

396
00:21:57,254 --> 00:22:00,056
But you know,
if you take a long time thinking over

397
00:22:00,123 --> 00:22:03,927
what you want to say, it's more likely
the other person will understand you.

398
00:22:05,662 --> 00:22:08,698
What's important is good conversation.

399
00:22:08,765 --> 00:22:12,436
Sometimes, small talk
is necessary too, Hiroto.

400
00:22:13,103 --> 00:22:14,504
-Miss.
-Yes?

401
00:22:15,839 --> 00:22:17,841
What does "hypocrite" mean again?

402
00:22:17,908 --> 00:22:18,875
What?

403
00:22:21,178 --> 00:22:22,512
Oh, I remember.

404
00:22:24,114 --> 00:22:25,615
A hypocrite.

405
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:39,796
Seriously, why does it always
turn out like this?

406
00:22:40,363 --> 00:22:42,065
Please cheer up.

407
00:22:42,132 --> 00:22:45,836
As the person responsible for calling you
to this school, I will do something.

408
00:22:46,703 --> 00:22:47,938
But still,

409
00:22:48,004 --> 00:22:52,108
are you confident you can persuade
that pushy parent, Ryunosuke?

410
00:22:52,175 --> 00:22:53,777
Not really…

411
00:22:53,844 --> 00:22:57,814
If I'm going to get fired anyway,
maybe I should just quit on my own?

412
00:22:57,881 --> 00:23:00,717
No, don't get so desperate.

413
00:23:00,784 --> 00:23:05,088
Let's make everyone see that only you
can be Class 1-B's homeroom teacher.

414
00:23:05,155 --> 00:23:06,089
How?

415
00:23:06,857 --> 00:23:09,993
For now, since that father
seems difficult,

416
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:13,997
wouldn't it be better to persuade Hiroto
and have him return to the soccer club?

417
00:23:15,799 --> 00:23:16,733
I see.

418
00:23:18,468 --> 00:23:21,505
All right, I have a good idea.

419
00:23:30,547 --> 00:23:31,715
Hey.

420
00:23:32,449 --> 00:23:34,284
Why aren't you training?

421
00:23:34,351 --> 00:23:36,920
You can do strength training
while your hand is fractured.

422
00:23:37,754 --> 00:23:38,722
I know that.

423
00:23:38,788 --> 00:23:43,426
The reason things turned out like this
is because you play goalkeeper!

424
00:23:44,427 --> 00:23:48,498
If you had played forward like I told you,
this wouldn't have happened!

425
00:23:48,565 --> 00:23:49,733
Oh!

426
00:23:49,799 --> 00:23:52,569
It's a good opportunity,
so switch to playing forward, okay?

427
00:23:53,336 --> 00:23:54,404
I…

428
00:23:55,071 --> 00:23:56,072
What?

429
00:23:58,341 --> 00:24:00,911
No, you wouldn't understand anyway.

430
00:24:00,977 --> 00:24:02,546
Hey, Hiroto!

431
00:24:02,612 --> 00:24:05,315
Hey, wait!

432
00:24:05,382 --> 00:24:06,550
Let me go!

433
00:24:06,616 --> 00:24:08,118
What's with that attitude?

434
00:24:08,184 --> 00:24:09,519
What are you going to do?

435
00:24:12,789 --> 00:24:15,592
Please stop it. He's injured!

436
00:24:15,659 --> 00:24:18,161
Who do you think made it
so you could make it this far?

437
00:24:19,229 --> 00:24:22,465
You were born to a talented soccer player,

438
00:24:22,532 --> 00:24:24,301
so be more grateful for it!

439
00:24:27,070 --> 00:24:28,638
Are you okay, Hiroto?

440
00:24:30,206 --> 00:24:31,741
I'm sick and tired of this.

441
00:24:32,375 --> 00:24:34,611
Sick of this house and school!

442
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:37,247
Hiroto!

443
00:24:45,088 --> 00:24:46,590
What are you doing here?

444
00:24:46,656 --> 00:24:48,058
What about you?

445
00:24:48,925 --> 00:24:50,026
Nothing, really.

446
00:24:50,627 --> 00:24:52,862
I've got nothing left to do anyway.

447
00:24:52,929 --> 00:24:53,964
You…

448
00:24:55,298 --> 00:24:57,167
Will you be okay like this?

449
00:24:57,867 --> 00:24:58,735
What?

450
00:24:59,302 --> 00:25:02,072
Are you worried about me?
Just because we're classmates?

451
00:25:02,606 --> 00:25:04,374
Not really, it's nothing like that.

452
00:25:06,109 --> 00:25:09,112
Hey, Soma.

453
00:25:11,314 --> 00:25:14,651
Is it true that you repeated a year?

454
00:25:16,686 --> 00:25:18,421
What's it to you?

455
00:25:19,122 --> 00:25:20,090
Nothing.

456
00:25:20,957 --> 00:25:22,092
I'm just bored.

457
00:25:23,326 --> 00:25:26,329
Thought you might know
about something interesting.

458
00:25:26,896 --> 00:25:28,331
What do you mean?

459
00:25:30,233 --> 00:25:31,334
For example…

460
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:34,771
Weed,

461
00:25:36,806 --> 00:25:38,008
or gummies…

462
00:25:39,075 --> 00:25:40,844
FUSION CUISINE

463
00:25:40,910 --> 00:25:42,412
Oh, we were waiting!

464
00:25:42,479 --> 00:25:44,247
Here are your two beers.

465
00:25:44,314 --> 00:25:47,217
What? Why are you here, Masaru?
Where is Murai?

466
00:25:47,283 --> 00:25:51,021
That idiot is out with a cold.
So I'm here helping out.

467
00:25:51,087 --> 00:25:52,589
Pathetic.

468
00:25:52,656 --> 00:25:55,458
This guy's Masaru.
A student of mine, same as you.

469
00:25:56,159 --> 00:25:57,827
Hello, I'm Ryunosuke Miyazawa.

470
00:25:58,662 --> 00:26:00,830
Didn't we meet during
the drill and rain-making?

471
00:26:00,897 --> 00:26:01,965
-Yes, we did.
-Right?

472
00:26:02,032 --> 00:26:03,533
He's your student?

473
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:07,170
Yeah, now he's an elite
working for our school's parent company.

474
00:26:07,237 --> 00:26:10,507
Wow, even though you had
a mess like him as your teacher,

475
00:26:10,573 --> 00:26:13,576
you still grew up to be a fine young man!

476
00:26:13,643 --> 00:26:16,046
Shut up, you. A customer is calling you.

477
00:26:16,112 --> 00:26:19,182
Oh, right. Onicchi. My daughter told me…

478
00:26:19,249 --> 00:26:21,084
Did you cause trouble again?

479
00:26:21,151 --> 00:26:23,353
Don't get fired, or Ms. Fuyutsuki
will divorce you!

480
00:26:23,420 --> 00:26:25,288
Fine, I get it. Shoo.

481
00:26:25,355 --> 00:26:27,290
There you go, shooing me away.

482
00:26:27,957 --> 00:26:29,092
Come on, let's toast.

483
00:26:29,159 --> 00:26:29,993
Yes.

484
00:26:30,727 --> 00:26:31,661
Cheers.

485
00:26:39,169 --> 00:26:40,870
-Oh, by the way…
-What?

486
00:26:40,937 --> 00:26:42,639
You said you had a good idea?

487
00:26:42,706 --> 00:26:46,242
No, I thought if we had some drinks
and talked about it,

488
00:26:46,309 --> 00:26:49,079
a good solution would definitely come up.

489
00:26:49,145 --> 00:26:50,146
I see.

490
00:26:51,414 --> 00:26:54,250
Damn it, right when
we were getting started.

491
00:26:54,951 --> 00:26:55,785
What?

492
00:26:57,687 --> 00:26:58,855
What's wrong, Soma?

493
00:26:58,922 --> 00:27:01,991
I ran into Hiroto just now.

494
00:27:02,559 --> 00:27:04,027
Yeah? And?

495
00:27:04,094 --> 00:27:06,296
He seemed desperate.

496
00:27:06,863 --> 00:27:08,665
I feel he's about to do
something dangerous.

497
00:27:09,699 --> 00:27:10,800
What?

498
00:27:13,136 --> 00:27:14,170
Hey!

499
00:27:14,771 --> 00:27:17,640
Watch where you're walking, you damn brat!

500
00:27:17,707 --> 00:27:19,042
Watch out, okay?

501
00:27:22,912 --> 00:27:25,081
ALCOHOL

502
00:27:25,148 --> 00:27:26,916
NO SELLING TO MINORS

503
00:27:31,654 --> 00:27:33,323
Hey!

504
00:27:33,890 --> 00:27:36,025
What are you doing?
You're still in high school.

505
00:27:36,092 --> 00:27:37,393
What does it matter?

506
00:27:38,261 --> 00:27:39,596
I'll quit that school anyway.

507
00:27:40,163 --> 00:27:41,131
Wait.

508
00:27:41,197 --> 00:27:42,499
What gives? Let me go!

509
00:27:42,565 --> 00:27:44,167
All right.

510
00:27:44,234 --> 00:27:48,238
Want to go give it a final farewell?
Looks like I'll get fired too.

511
00:27:48,304 --> 00:27:49,239
What?

512
00:27:54,077 --> 00:27:56,079
How about a toast, with this?

513
00:28:01,785 --> 00:28:04,187
What are we going to do? It's closed.

514
00:28:04,254 --> 00:28:05,421
Let's go.

515
00:28:10,860 --> 00:28:11,694
Come on.

516
00:28:12,929 --> 00:28:14,130
Is this really okay?

517
00:28:14,197 --> 00:28:15,465
It's fine!

518
00:28:15,532 --> 00:28:18,935
I used to do this all the time
back in the day. So nostalgic.

519
00:28:19,002 --> 00:28:20,103
What the heck?

520
00:28:22,539 --> 00:28:25,809
So, what now? Want to break a window?

521
00:28:26,442 --> 00:28:28,945
No, that'd be bad.

522
00:28:29,946 --> 00:28:32,115
Want to shout at the top of our lungs?

523
00:28:32,182 --> 00:28:34,317
Or maybe go streaking?

524
00:28:34,951 --> 00:28:35,919
I don't get you at all.

525
00:28:35,985 --> 00:28:39,756
What's with you? Kids these days…

526
00:28:40,356 --> 00:28:41,658
They can't have fun at all.

527
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:46,229
Wait, weren't we going to toast?

528
00:28:48,331 --> 00:28:50,867
Idiot! Like I'd let a minor
drink alcohol! So good!

529
00:28:50,934 --> 00:28:52,402
What's that about?

530
00:28:52,936 --> 00:28:54,671
Nothing you say makes any sense!

531
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,641
Hey.

532
00:28:59,943 --> 00:29:00,977
Want to have a match?

533
00:29:01,644 --> 00:29:02,579
A match?

534
00:29:02,645 --> 00:29:04,280
A penalty shootout.

535
00:29:04,347 --> 00:29:07,884
Since you're injured, I'll be the keeper.

536
00:29:08,751 --> 00:29:10,687
If I stop your shot,

537
00:29:12,322 --> 00:29:15,191
you apologize to the team
and go back to the soccer club.

538
00:29:16,259 --> 00:29:17,360
And if I win?

539
00:29:17,927 --> 00:29:19,696
I will grovel before your old man.

540
00:29:20,396 --> 00:29:24,067
I'll say, "I'm quitting school,
so please forgive me."

541
00:29:32,909 --> 00:29:34,911
You think I can't shoot
because I'm a keeper, huh?

542
00:29:34,978 --> 00:29:36,412
Not bad.

543
00:29:36,479 --> 00:29:38,781
All right, let's do it!

544
00:29:40,283 --> 00:29:43,019
This is nice!
This is what youth is all about!

545
00:29:43,086 --> 00:29:45,521
Stop talking nonsense!

546
00:29:48,458 --> 00:29:49,726
What on earth are you doing?

547
00:29:52,762 --> 00:29:53,930
Hiroto!

548
00:29:53,997 --> 00:29:55,398
-We have to run!
-What?

549
00:29:55,965 --> 00:29:57,367
Hey! Stop!

550
00:30:17,153 --> 00:30:19,455
Let's hide here for a bit.

551
00:30:20,089 --> 00:30:23,927
I don't think we needed to run.
You're a teacher, after all.

552
00:30:23,993 --> 00:30:26,829
Oh, right. I forgot.

553
00:30:27,997 --> 00:30:29,899
-What's wrong with you?
-Wait a second.

554
00:30:30,566 --> 00:30:31,434
Oh, no.

555
00:30:31,501 --> 00:30:34,437
I forgot the beer too. What a waste.

556
00:30:34,504 --> 00:30:37,307
Anyway, I won that match.

557
00:30:37,373 --> 00:30:39,509
-It doesn't count!
-What?

558
00:30:39,575 --> 00:30:43,112
Right when I was about to make
a cool save, someone interrupted us!

559
00:30:43,179 --> 00:30:45,415
No way, the ball went in way before that.

560
00:30:45,481 --> 00:30:48,818
You're so young, don't worry
about small details like that.

561
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:52,121
But, still…

562
00:30:52,689 --> 00:30:54,390
Being a keeper must be tough.

563
00:30:55,158 --> 00:30:58,661
Having to stop a ball
kicked from that close.

564
00:31:01,030 --> 00:31:02,165
Well, yeah.

565
00:31:02,732 --> 00:31:07,170
So, why did you decide to be a keeper?

566
00:31:08,738 --> 00:31:09,572
You know…

567
00:31:10,673 --> 00:31:11,574
Yes?

568
00:31:12,175 --> 00:31:14,644
I hate being asked "why"
more than anything.

569
00:31:15,211 --> 00:31:18,014
"Why," huh. For what reason?

570
00:31:19,315 --> 00:31:21,084
It's my father's favorite phrase.

571
00:31:22,151 --> 00:31:24,687
Since I was little, whenever anything
happened, he would say it.

572
00:31:25,521 --> 00:31:27,657
"Why won't you do as I say?"

573
00:31:29,459 --> 00:31:31,794
"Why am I angry, do you know?"

574
00:31:32,395 --> 00:31:34,230
"Why did you let me down?"

575
00:31:34,297 --> 00:31:37,133
"Why, why, why…"

576
00:31:39,402 --> 00:31:42,672
Sounds like something he'd say.

577
00:31:42,739 --> 00:31:43,706
That's why

578
00:31:45,141 --> 00:31:48,745
I tried so hard,
desperate to please my father.

579
00:31:51,381 --> 00:31:54,784
I didn't have time to care about
the people around me, and…

580
00:31:55,651 --> 00:31:56,619
And?

581
00:32:01,391 --> 00:32:02,825
The more I did it,

582
00:32:05,395 --> 00:32:07,130
the more I fell in love

583
00:32:08,798 --> 00:32:10,299
with the keeper position.

584
00:32:11,934 --> 00:32:14,971
Those feelings of yours,

585
00:32:16,205 --> 00:32:18,841
you've got to convey them
to him. To your dad.

586
00:32:21,144 --> 00:32:22,779
He won't understand.

587
00:32:24,013 --> 00:32:25,448
It'll be fine.

588
00:32:26,482 --> 00:32:29,552
I have a good idea.

589
00:32:29,619 --> 00:32:32,221
HOSOKAWA

590
00:32:32,789 --> 00:32:35,324
Why do I have to come along too?

591
00:32:36,659 --> 00:32:38,027
Please.

592
00:32:38,094 --> 00:32:41,264
If you talk to him as
the interim homeroom teacher,

593
00:32:41,330 --> 00:32:43,866
that man might actually listen.

594
00:32:43,933 --> 00:32:46,869
Also, if I go alone

595
00:32:46,936 --> 00:32:50,973
and say something careless, and he
barges into the school again, it'd be bad.

596
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:52,308
I suppose so, but…

597
00:32:53,709 --> 00:32:56,946
Hiroto, I was worried about you.

598
00:32:58,214 --> 00:32:59,082
Who are you?

599
00:32:59,148 --> 00:33:02,418
I'm Kashiwabara, the acting homeroom
teacher for your son's class.

600
00:33:03,086 --> 00:33:04,487
I'm Eikichi Onizuka.

601
00:33:08,524 --> 00:33:10,293
Don't dump everything on me!

602
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:13,996
Excuses won't cut it,
get it done right by tomorrow!

603
00:33:14,063 --> 00:33:15,098
Oh, jeez.

604
00:33:15,765 --> 00:33:16,666
Dear.

605
00:33:16,732 --> 00:33:19,802
Hiroto is back.
His school teachers are with him too.

606
00:33:21,370 --> 00:33:24,140
What on earth do you think
you're doing? You made us worry.

607
00:33:25,541 --> 00:33:26,676
I'm sorry.

608
00:33:32,248 --> 00:33:33,616
Sir…

609
00:33:34,183 --> 00:33:37,453
Could you please listen
to what Hiroto has to say?

610
00:33:38,221 --> 00:33:40,123
Why should I do that?

611
00:33:40,723 --> 00:33:43,593
Your son hasn't been able to express

612
00:33:43,659 --> 00:33:47,730
his true feelings to you until now,
but he has realized that it isn't good.

613
00:33:47,797 --> 00:33:49,265
Right?

614
00:33:50,266 --> 00:33:51,167
Yeah.

615
00:33:52,835 --> 00:33:55,404
Dear, listen to him.

616
00:33:58,040 --> 00:34:00,176
If you have something to say,
make it quick.

617
00:34:00,877 --> 00:34:04,747
I understand
that you wanted me to play forward,

618
00:34:06,115 --> 00:34:09,285
and I'm grateful for everything
you've taught me about soccer.

619
00:34:10,453 --> 00:34:11,554
But I really…

620
00:34:13,156 --> 00:34:15,024
want to play as a keeper.

621
00:34:15,625 --> 00:34:16,592
Why?

622
00:34:18,895 --> 00:34:22,498
I'm not that smart,
so I can't express myself properly,

623
00:34:24,433 --> 00:34:26,469
but I feel like it's what I'm meant to do.

624
00:34:26,536 --> 00:34:27,603
But why?

625
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:30,806
I told you, it's because…

626
00:34:32,575 --> 00:34:33,910
Enough already!

627
00:34:35,278 --> 00:34:38,915
You're still just a child,
so shut up and do as you're told!

628
00:34:39,916 --> 00:34:41,350
Oh, yeah.

629
00:34:42,151 --> 00:34:43,886
This is a good opportunity.

630
00:34:43,953 --> 00:34:47,990
Quit that high school
and transfer to the one I choose.

631
00:34:48,057 --> 00:34:48,891
What?

632
00:34:48,958 --> 00:34:50,359
Hey, please wait!

633
00:34:50,426 --> 00:34:52,395
I'm busy here. Please leave now.

634
00:34:55,565 --> 00:34:58,134
This is why I hate adults.

635
00:34:58,201 --> 00:35:00,036
What? So you were here too?

636
00:35:00,102 --> 00:35:01,070
Gosh…

637
00:35:02,004 --> 00:35:04,207
Always complaining about everything we do,

638
00:35:05,141 --> 00:35:07,643
telling us to shut up
and just do what you say…

639
00:35:07,710 --> 00:35:10,179
Saying stuff like,
"There's no way you can do it."

640
00:35:10,246 --> 00:35:13,616
Always dragging people down.

641
00:35:16,419 --> 00:35:19,188
Hiroto's life is his and his alone.

642
00:35:20,256 --> 00:35:22,892
It's not to fulfill the hopes
of adults like you!

643
00:35:24,260 --> 00:35:25,194
Besides,

644
00:35:25,761 --> 00:35:27,897
Hiroto is still only 16!

645
00:35:28,631 --> 00:35:31,567
It's natural that he can't explain
everything perfectly!

646
00:35:32,735 --> 00:35:37,974
Taking the time to listen to him
is a parent's job!

647
00:35:38,874 --> 00:35:42,311
And yet you just sit there
acting all high and mighty,

648
00:35:42,378 --> 00:35:45,815
spewing boring bullshit on and on!

649
00:35:47,350 --> 00:35:51,454
Why can't you just cheer us on
for what we want to do?

650
00:35:52,321 --> 00:35:53,389
You…

651
00:35:55,191 --> 00:35:56,759
You old bastard!

652
00:36:02,031 --> 00:36:04,667
Get out of here!

653
00:36:09,405 --> 00:36:10,273
Scary.

654
00:36:11,641 --> 00:36:13,809
Weren't you supposed to leave it to me?

655
00:36:14,710 --> 00:36:17,713
What about you? Why didn't you stop me?

656
00:36:17,780 --> 00:36:21,250
You were already yelling
before I could do anything! Like a kid!

657
00:36:21,317 --> 00:36:22,918
What should we do now?

658
00:36:22,985 --> 00:36:26,555
Should we go back inside and apologize?

659
00:36:26,622 --> 00:36:28,224
What? Are you kidding me…

660
00:36:30,926 --> 00:36:31,594
Huh?

661
00:36:32,628 --> 00:36:33,529
That is…

662
00:36:34,597 --> 00:36:35,898
Ms. Koizumi.

663
00:36:53,249 --> 00:36:54,283
Hiroto!

664
00:36:54,350 --> 00:36:55,584
Ms. Koizumi!

665
00:36:59,088 --> 00:37:00,156
Are you okay?

666
00:37:01,223 --> 00:37:02,525
What about you?

667
00:37:09,799 --> 00:37:11,767
Is your hand okay? Does it hurt?

668
00:37:14,036 --> 00:37:14,970
I'm fine.

669
00:37:18,341 --> 00:37:19,742
I'm sorry, Hiroto.

670
00:37:21,444 --> 00:37:22,645
Lately,

671
00:37:23,813 --> 00:37:27,316
I've only been thinking
about my own career.

672
00:37:30,286 --> 00:37:32,388
Being the advisor for the soccer club too…

673
00:37:32,988 --> 00:37:36,092
"If a woman does it,
it will draw more attention."

674
00:37:36,158 --> 00:37:38,394
Is how I proposed it
to the Vice Principal.

675
00:37:38,928 --> 00:37:42,832
Somewhere along the way, I feel like
I was just doing it to gain popularity.

676
00:37:44,667 --> 00:37:45,668
So,

677
00:37:47,269 --> 00:37:49,505
when you were facing such a major crisis,

678
00:37:50,039 --> 00:37:55,378
I forgot to tell you
the most important thing, as a teacher.

679
00:37:56,612 --> 00:37:58,280
What is that?

680
00:38:00,216 --> 00:38:01,550
I have always

681
00:38:03,018 --> 00:38:06,756
respected you for working so hard.

682
00:38:10,426 --> 00:38:11,694
But listen, Hiroto.

683
00:38:12,461 --> 00:38:15,131
Right now, the most important thing

684
00:38:16,665 --> 00:38:19,468
is to take a deep breath and calm down.

685
00:38:21,036 --> 00:38:22,037
And…

686
00:38:22,671 --> 00:38:26,075
to let us help you,
so you can keep giving it your all,

687
00:38:26,142 --> 00:38:27,877
like you always have.

688
00:38:29,044 --> 00:38:30,012
Okay?

689
00:38:31,881 --> 00:38:34,016
Amazing, Ms. Koizumi.

690
00:38:34,550 --> 00:38:35,384
Well said.

691
00:38:35,951 --> 00:38:37,720
Please stop it.

692
00:38:37,787 --> 00:38:40,990
You know, Ms. Kashiwabara
scolded me earlier.

693
00:38:41,690 --> 00:38:44,693
She said, "The old you
was a much better teacher."

694
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:46,729
No way. How harsh.

695
00:38:46,796 --> 00:38:48,898
Hey, wait!
I didn't put it quite like that…

696
00:38:48,964 --> 00:38:50,032
Then,

697
00:38:50,666 --> 00:38:52,968
Ms. Kashiwabara, don't fall behind!

698
00:38:53,803 --> 00:38:56,405
Say something to Hiroto too!

699
00:38:56,472 --> 00:38:58,941
Don't put me on the spot
in a situation like this!

700
00:38:59,008 --> 00:39:01,310
Please say something, Ms. Kashiwabara.

701
00:39:01,377 --> 00:39:02,311
What?

702
00:39:04,413 --> 00:39:05,581
Well…

703
00:39:07,883 --> 00:39:11,387
In a book I read once,
it said something like this.

704
00:39:12,021 --> 00:39:13,722
"Goalkeeper might be a position

705
00:39:14,256 --> 00:39:17,092
that can only be played
by someone with the courage

706
00:39:17,159 --> 00:39:18,894
to put their own body on the line."

707
00:39:20,830 --> 00:39:22,064
I think you play keeper

708
00:39:22,631 --> 00:39:26,235
because you want to protect
the people who are precious to you.

709
00:39:32,441 --> 00:39:36,378
Well then, let's keep
playing soccer, Hiroto.

710
00:39:37,713 --> 00:39:38,747
Okay?

711
00:39:38,814 --> 00:39:40,716
The reason you've made it this far

712
00:39:41,917 --> 00:39:45,087
is because you have an incredible talent.

713
00:39:47,623 --> 00:39:51,360
It's because you worked
many times harder than anyone else!

714
00:39:52,628 --> 00:39:55,831
It wasn't because your dad gave it to you,
or something like that.

715
00:39:56,866 --> 00:39:57,700
Right?

716
00:40:20,322 --> 00:40:21,156
I…

717
00:40:24,827 --> 00:40:27,162
Instead of just
blaming people like you, Father,

718
00:40:27,730 --> 00:40:30,432
I want to be someone
who protects those precious to me.

719
00:40:31,500 --> 00:40:32,635
What did you say?

720
00:40:33,669 --> 00:40:36,705
Even when we lost a match
or when I made a mistake,

721
00:40:36,772 --> 00:40:39,708
she always told me
I was the coolest one out there.

722
00:40:41,810 --> 00:40:44,847
I want to become someone
who can protect people, just like Mom.

723
00:40:46,682 --> 00:40:47,683
That's why

724
00:40:50,052 --> 00:40:51,420
I'm not transferring,

725
00:40:53,789 --> 00:40:55,324
and I'm not quitting as keeper.

726
00:40:58,794 --> 00:41:00,329
Because this is who I am.

727
00:41:05,501 --> 00:41:07,770
One, two!

728
00:41:07,836 --> 00:41:10,205
One, two!

729
00:41:17,179 --> 00:41:18,280
Would you…

730
00:41:22,418 --> 00:41:24,720
let me play soccer with all of you again?

731
00:41:29,124 --> 00:41:30,092
Please.

732
00:41:35,364 --> 00:41:38,267
All right, next up, Eita,
let's move on to step work!

733
00:41:38,334 --> 00:41:40,102
Okay!

734
00:41:40,169 --> 00:41:41,403
Nice!

735
00:41:41,971 --> 00:41:44,940
I'm so glad for Hiroto.
It's like the weight has been lifted.

736
00:41:45,007 --> 00:41:50,012
Could this be
what they call "a blessing in disguise"?

737
00:41:51,680 --> 00:41:54,950
Can you stop with that
"I said something impressive" face?

738
00:41:55,017 --> 00:41:55,918
Yes.

739
00:42:01,290 --> 00:42:02,524
-Mr. Onizuka.
-Yes?

740
00:42:03,592 --> 00:42:06,095
Don't forget what you said earlier.

741
00:42:06,161 --> 00:42:07,696
Yeah, I know.

742
00:42:10,933 --> 00:42:13,402
What did you tell him earlier?

743
00:42:14,103 --> 00:42:15,771
We made a promise.

744
00:42:16,338 --> 00:42:20,075
That when Hiroto grows up,
we'll go out drinking together.

745
00:42:22,344 --> 00:42:23,245
I see.

746
00:42:24,079 --> 00:42:24,913
Mr. Onizuka.

747
00:42:27,683 --> 00:42:29,418
You can resume
as homeroom teacher tomorrow.

748
00:42:29,485 --> 00:42:31,954
What? Seriously?

749
00:42:32,021 --> 00:42:34,757
Hiroto's mother got in touch with us.

750
00:42:34,823 --> 00:42:37,926
She said her son is blessed
to have two wonderful teachers.

751
00:42:38,994 --> 00:42:41,263
I see. Wait!

752
00:42:41,330 --> 00:42:44,299
Who are these "two teachers"?

753
00:42:44,366 --> 00:42:47,369
She actually said "two ladies,"
so maybe Ms. Koizumi and me.

754
00:42:47,436 --> 00:42:48,704
What?

755
00:42:48,771 --> 00:42:51,540
I worked pretty hard too, you know!

756
00:42:51,607 --> 00:42:54,376
I guess your good qualities
are just hard to convey, Mr. Onizuka.

757
00:42:54,443 --> 00:42:55,811
That's weird.

758
00:42:56,311 --> 00:42:57,479
Mr. Onizuka.

759
00:43:04,620 --> 00:43:06,689
Wait, what did you just say?

760
00:43:07,256 --> 00:43:08,524
Please tell me!

761
00:43:10,292 --> 00:43:11,427
"Please forgive

762
00:43:11,493 --> 00:43:14,897
my immaturity, for not recognizing you
as a teacher until now."

763
00:43:16,031 --> 00:43:17,433
-What?
-That's what she said.

764
00:43:29,611 --> 00:43:31,547
THE NEW TERM HAS BEGUN!

765
00:43:37,286 --> 00:43:38,620
Ken-Ken, you can't swim?

766
00:43:38,687 --> 00:43:40,556
-I can.
-You can't!

767
00:43:40,622 --> 00:43:42,057
-Hey!
-You suck at it.

768
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:46,361
-Will you let me join the Drill Team?
-No way!

769
00:43:46,428 --> 00:43:47,763
Are you really sure?

770
00:43:48,564 --> 00:43:49,398
Yes.

771
00:43:49,465 --> 00:43:51,400
Awesome! We finally got five people!

772
00:43:51,467 --> 00:43:53,402
-Great!
-Yes!

773
00:43:53,469 --> 00:43:54,503
-Hurray!
-Yes!

774
00:43:54,570 --> 00:43:55,771
But!

775
00:43:55,838 --> 00:43:58,006
I will also be in the soccer club.

776
00:43:59,007 --> 00:43:59,842
No way!

777
00:43:59,908 --> 00:44:00,976
What?

778
00:44:01,043 --> 00:44:04,780
We are serious about our club too.
Like you are with soccer, Hiroto.

779
00:44:04,847 --> 00:44:05,781
Right?

780
00:44:06,315 --> 00:44:07,149
Yes.

781
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:10,052
You guys are something else.

782
00:44:10,619 --> 00:44:13,222
But we appreciate the thought. Thank you.

783
00:44:14,256 --> 00:44:16,391
Oh, right! Let's give Hiroto a nickname!

784
00:44:16,925 --> 00:44:18,193
Hey, what do you like?

785
00:44:18,894 --> 00:44:19,862
Anything is fine.

786
00:44:19,928 --> 00:44:22,865
Then "Anything is Fine" it is!
Hey, Anything is Fine!

787
00:44:22,931 --> 00:44:24,533
No, that's not what I meant!

788
00:44:24,600 --> 00:44:27,136
Well, how about Hero? Sounds like Hiroto.

789
00:44:27,202 --> 00:44:28,737
Oh, that's good!

790
00:44:29,438 --> 00:44:30,639
Yo, Hero!

791
00:44:31,206 --> 00:44:33,041
Hero!

792
00:44:33,108 --> 00:44:34,610
Sit down.

793
00:44:35,310 --> 00:44:36,612
We're starting homeroom.

794
00:44:41,683 --> 00:44:43,185
Mr. Onizuka

795
00:44:44,620 --> 00:44:47,489
is taking today off.

796
00:44:48,056 --> 00:44:49,925
-What?
-Why?

797
00:44:56,498 --> 00:44:57,833
To be honest…

798
00:45:00,469 --> 00:45:01,970
You may be Onizuka's henchman…

799
00:45:02,037 --> 00:45:03,105
Just leave me alone already!

800
00:45:03,172 --> 00:45:04,807
I wish he would take off forever.

801
00:45:04,873 --> 00:45:07,609
Do what you want. If you don't
want to come to school, don't!

802
00:45:07,676 --> 00:45:09,378
I'm quitting teaching anyway.

803
00:45:10,078 --> 00:45:11,814
Are you doing sugar dating?

804
00:45:11,880 --> 00:45:12,748
Give it back!

805
00:45:12,815 --> 00:45:15,250
-What happened?
-I didn't see anything…

806
00:45:15,317 --> 00:45:16,819
Actually, I…

807
00:45:16,885 --> 00:45:18,487
I have a wife!

808
00:45:18,554 --> 00:45:20,689
If that's how you feel, Miss…

809
00:45:20,756 --> 00:45:23,192
Having to deal with brats who have
absurdly high pride and nothing else…

810
00:45:23,258 --> 00:45:25,027
I messed up big time.

811
00:45:25,961 --> 00:45:28,030
Sorry for making you wait!

812
00:45:28,096 --> 00:45:29,064
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

